WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:15.090
It’s project time! Build a helpful assistant app: ask at least two questions, store the answers in variables, calculate with operators, decide with if/else, reply with a joined message, and validate odd inputs.

2
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:24.340
Build a helpful assistant: a study timer planner, a pocket-money calculator, a recipe scaler, a fitness helper — your choice.

3
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:33.840
Every app follows this pattern: get input (ask), process it (variables, operators, decisions), and give output (say).

4
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.430
Users type surprising things.

5
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:42.410
Check the input is sensible (e.g. not negative) and respond kindly if it isn’t.

6
00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.050
Write a test table: input, expected output, actual output.

7
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.450
Include normal, boundary and invalid inputs.

8
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.670
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

9
00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:56.410
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
